      "writtenOn": "2024-11-22T14:34:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "While this approach works, I think we could try to make CommandRecordingContext a bit smarter instead to avoid the need to expose all these flags/mask/stages outside of buffer.\n\n```\nstruct CommandRecordingContext {\npublic:\n  AddBufferBarrier(srcAccessMask, dstAccessMask, srcStages, dstStages, shaderStage)\n  EmitBufferBarriers();\n  \nprivate:\n  mBufferSrcAccessMask;\n  mBufferDstAccessMask;\n  ... (we might need to duplicate between vertex vs. the rest to avoid overflushing on tilers).\n}\n```\n\nThis way TransitionUsageNow would do:\n\n```\nTrackUsageAndAddResourceBarrier(recordingContext, usage, shaderStage);\nrecordingContext-\u003eEmitBufferBarriers();\n```",
      "revId": "d3b04d295da8b4135fb5bc169ae81599ea471367",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
